# The permission is "as though they didn't have hexproof", not "they lose hexproof" (CR 609.4, 702.11b): hexproof an opponent's
# creature gains after Nowhere to Run is on the battlefield is ignored too. Bot1's Nowhere to Run kills one of Bot2's two Elvish
# Mystics on turn three. On turn four Bot2 casts Snakeskin Veil on the other - the check shows it really has hexproof - and
# Bot1's Lightning Bolt, cast once the Veil has resolved, is aimed at it all the same and kills the 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Nowhere to Run
Lightning Bolt
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Elvish Mystic
Elvish Mystic
Snakeskin Veil
Forest
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Snakeskin Veil.Cast(Elvish Mystic)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Keywords = Hexproof
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Elvish Mystic; Snakeskin Veil; Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
